# SROIE official-test35 category coverage reanalysis

Scope: same 35 official-test documents selected in sroie_external35_selection.csv; 7 per role, 28 positive pages and 7 negative controls, 77 annotated synthetic PII entities. Utility summary from the historical 175 inferences matches manuscript Table 7 (Original .6071428571; Strong and RA .6357142857). This is distinct from the older pilot with 20 train and 15 test pages and the newly specified conservative C2 350-page experiment.

Inputs: SROIE-PII-full971-metadata.zip; SROIE-external-full971-results-metadata (1).zip; official test35 selection CSV and protocol. Text-free selected derivatives are in coordinates_35.json. Recorded policy action rectangles for Strong and historical Risk-adaptive C2 are used. Non-RETAIN action rectangles count as spatial intervention regions, including TOKENIZE and PARTIAL_MASK; geometric coverage is not optical opacity, unreadability or re-identification prevention. No new rendering, OCR or Donut inference performed.

Geometry: continuous/half-open rectangles (width=x2-x1; height=y2-y1), union intersections counted once. All rectangles verified valid and within image bounds. Overall coverage is equal-weighted over 77 entities. Negative controls have no coverage value and are excluded from the entity denominator, but all 35 pages contribute to mean masked-page-area. Relative area reduction is 1-mean(RA area)/mean(Strong area).

95% percentile confidence intervals: paired resampling of all 35 documents, retaining all entities from each sampled document, 20000 draws, NumPy default_rng seed 20261004. Category means are pooled entity means in each draw; draws without any entity in the category are excluded. Zero-width sample bootstrap intervals in completely covered strata do not imply population-level certainty.

Priority groups use historical P3_HIGH/P4_CRITICAL annotations, not G1-G3. Historical PARTIAL_MASK actions on name/phone explain geometric deficits; this is not validation of the general mandatory-full-masking G1 rule.

Audit: Manuscript correspondence: This reanalysis provides the revised SROIE spatial results in Table 6 and the entity-type and experimental protection-priority results in Tables 17 and 18. Strong coverage is 1.0000 and Risk-adaptive coverage is 0.9591, with a difference of −0.0409 (95% CI: [−0.0620, −0.0180]) and a relative masked-page-area reduction of 4.46%. The analysis uses archived coordinates and does not independently validate rendered pixels or re-identification protection.

Reproduce: install numpy and execute python reproduce.py. Source image bytes and full text metadata are not included.
